I began thinking of polearms in terms parallel to daggers -

Why do I collect and throw/wield orcish daggers?  Because they are
common early on and hits with them apply to the better daggers.  But
once I have a "dozen" daggers of all types every one I encounter
that's
a better type I stash an orcish dagger.  Why do I collect and throw/
wield
regular daggers?  Same deal until I gradually replace them with elven
daggers.  Why do I stick with elven daggers and not switch to silver
daggers?  Because the silver daggers are rare enough that I can't
ever expect to get a stack of a "dozen" highly enchanted silver
daggers
unless I want to do pudding farming or extinctionist.  Why don't I
ever
even try to replace my stack of elven/silver daggers with athames?
They are so rare I've never even checked if they stack.  But I'm sure
happy to keep any athame I find as a wielded or alternate wielded
weapon for it's non-combat abilities.

Basically with daggers there are 3 likely types in a natural
progression.
If I want to use polearms I look at damage and weight.  Halberd
doesn't even obviously win the damage race, but spetum beats them
all for damage/weight ratio.  So with polearms I'll use whichever one
I encounter first to exercise the skill.  When I encounter a new type
I look it up in the table to compare it's damage/weight ratio and
maybe
switch to it.  Once I get a spetum I lose interest in any other non-
artifact
polearm that isn't another spetum of better enchantment.  Getting a
+5 polearm as a gift (are Spork gifts fooproof?) is close enough to an
artifact for my purposes ...

So any more than 3-4 types of polearms is just noise.  Trolls get
25% chance of a list of 4, plenty enough variety for polearms.

In SCA combat polearms depend on soldiers working in two ranks.
The front rank is shield bearers with one-handed weapons.  Maybe
axes used like grappling hooks to pull the shields from the opponents.
The back rank is two-handed wielders with various sorts of weapons
reaching past the first rank.  The control of pets is too poor to use
them
as a front rank of shield bearers so polearms aren't as effective in
Nethack as they are in the SCA.

